UID:transmediale-pro-helvetia-digital-art-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T205315Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Deadline: transmediale x Pro Helvetia Digital Art Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:The fifth iteration of transmediale's Digital Art Residency\, r
 un with the Swiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia\, awarded to one individual or
  collective working in digital art practices at the intersection of media 
 arts\, performance\, sound and moving image. THEME: the 2027 programme sit
 s under transmediale's 40th-anniversary framework RFC 40\, named after the
  early internet Request for Comments series\, and treats the festival as a
  counter-infrastructure: the call asks how a network stays legible to itse
 lf while surrounding structures break down\, and how technical paradigms c
 an be reconfigured into new cultural protocols outside extractive logics\,
  moving from critique to construction. Proposals should offer alternatives
  to how we understand\, respond to and shape the technological conditions 
 we inhabit. WHAT IS OFFERED: an artist fee of CHF 2\,000 per month for two
  months\; a CHF 15\,000 production grant supporting a new work or the cont
 inuation of an existing project\, open to all formats and building on the 
 research begun during the residency (the project must be completed by Dece
 mber 2027 at the latest)\; travel and accommodation for the festival and t
 he residency\; a shared modular working space at transmediale studio\; con
 nections to Berlin institutions and stakeholders\; a public presentation i
 n transmediale's year-round studio programme\; and the option of an online
  publication in transmediale's journal. STRUCTURE: kick-off with a present
 ation of the residency projects during transmediale 2027 (26 to 31 January
  2027\, attendance optional but strongly recommended)\; onboarding and the
  first hybrid stretch in May 2027\; the mandatory on-site month in Berlin 
 in June 2027\; and a second hybrid stretch including reporting in July 202
 7. Availability for the festival week and for the whole of June in Berlin 
 are treated as key prerequisites. TIMELINE: open call 16 July to 28 August
  2026 (23:59 CEST)\; selected residents announced October 2026. Applicatio
 ns are only accepted via transmediale's submission forms. Contact: info[at
 ]transmediale.de.\n\nOrganisation: transmediale (in cooperation with the S
 wiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia)\nLocation: Hybrid: remote plus on-site at 
 transmediale studio\, silent green Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germa
 ny. RESTRICTED: applicants must hold Swiss nationality or permanent reside
 nce in Switzerland and be firmly established in the Swiss cultural scene (
 Pro Helvetia's general requirements apply).\nAward: Artist fee of CHF 2\,0
 00 per month across the two-month residency (CHF 4\,000)\, plus a producti
 on grant of CHF 15\,000 for the selected project\, plus travel and accommo
 dation for both the festival and the residency month. Duos and collectives
  may apply but the fee and the production grant stay the same and must be 
 shared. No application fee.\nDuration: Two-month hybrid residency between 
 mid-May and mid-July 2027\, with the whole of June 2027 on-site in Berlin 
 (mandatory)\n\nMore: https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency
 -2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency-2027?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hybrid: remote plus on-site at transmediale studio\, silent green 
 Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germany. RESTRICTED: applicants must hol
 d Swiss nationality or permanent residence in Switzerland and be firmly es
 tablished in the Swiss cultural scene (Pro Helvetia's general requirements
  apply).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:transmediale-vilem-flusser-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T205315Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Deadline: Vilem Flusser Residency for Artistic Research 2027
DESCRIPTION:14th iteration of the residency collaboration between transmedi
 ale and the Vilem Flusser Archive at the Universitat der Kunste Berlin (Ud
 K)\, awarded to one Berlin-based artist-researcher working in digital art 
 and moving image practices\, design\, sound and media theory. Open to arti
 sts\, researchers\, practitioners\, designers\, filmmakers and sound artis
 ts across all formats. The two-month residency comes with an artist fee of
  EUR 1\,500 per residency month\; note there are NO funds for travel or ho
 using. Duos and collectives are welcome but share the same fee. Part of tr
 ansmediale's 2027 programme (40th anniversary\, themed 'RFC 40')\, seeking
  proposals that offer alternatives to how we understand\, respond to and s
 hape our technological conditions\, moving from critique to construction. 
 Deadline: 28 August 2026\, 23:59 CEST.\n\nOrganisation: transmediale and t
 he Vilem Flusser Archive\, Universitat der Kunste Berlin (UdK)\nLocation: 
 Berlin\, Germany (open to Berlin-based artist-researchers)\nAward: Two-mon
 th residency with an artist fee of EUR 1\,500 per residency month. NO fund
 s are available for travel or housing. For duos or collectives the fee rem
 ains the same and is shared. No application fee.\nDuration: Two-month resi
 dency\n\nMore: https://transmediale.de/en/news/vilem-flusser-residency-for
 -artistic-research-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://transmediale.de/en/news/vilem-flusser-residency-for-artistic-re
 search-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany (open to Berlin-based artist-researchers)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:francoise-cite-internationale-arts-clinique-2027@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T205315Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260816
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260817
SUMMARY:Deadline: Association Francoise pour l'oeuvre contemporaine x Cite 
 internationale des arts: Research and Creation Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:Launched in 2025\, this research and creation residency explore
 s the links between contemporary art\, psychiatry and the human sciences. 
 It is expressly not a therapeutic programme. It seeks artists whose practi
 ce resonates with the notion of the clinical\, meaning a situated approach
  that works closely with lived narratives and specific contexts\, and that
  engages with questions of care. The selected artist receives tailored sup
 port from Albertine de Galbert\, a clinical psychologist and exhibition cu
 rator\, including four to six working sessions\, alongside networking and 
 meeting time with programme partners. Outputs include an ongoing online jo
 urnal\, a mid-residency open studio\, and a closing presentation (exhibiti
 on\, public talk or publication) defined with the artist. Applications go 
 by email as a single PDF of no more than 15 MB to residence@francoiseartme
 mo.fr\, and require a two-page CV\, a ten-page portfolio\, a two-page stat
 ement of intent\, and a letter of recommendation from an institution or a 
 curator. A jury of four to six art and psychiatry specialists decides\, wi
 th results announced in September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Association Franc
 oise pour l'oeuvre contemporaine / Cite internationale des arts\nLocation:
  Paris\, France (Marais site of the Cite internationale des arts). Open to
  artist-authors of any nationality and any discipline\, mid-career or esta
 blished\, with no age limit. Applicants must be comfortable working in Fre
 nch or English. Note: the studio-apartments do not meet current accessibil
 ity standards for people with disabilities.\nAward: Grant of EUR 1\,000 ne
 t of tax per month\, plus a furnished studio-apartment (20 to 35 sq m\, co
 mbining living and working space)\, international return travel to Paris a
 irports or stations\, travel insurance\, and capped research support again
 st receipts. Additional fees apply for accompanying persons. No applicatio
 n fee.\nDuration: Approximately 12 weeks\, 5 January to 26 March 2027\n\nM
 ore: https://www.citeinternationaledesarts.fr/appels-a-candidature/associa
 tion-francoise-pour-loeuvre-contemporaine-x-cite-internationale-des-arts/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.citeinternationaledesarts.fr/appels-a-candidature/associati
 on-francoise-pour-loeuvre-contemporaine-x-cite-internationale-des-arts/?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Paris\, France (Marais site of the Cite internationale des arts). 
 Open to artist-authors of any nationality and any discipline\, mid-career 
 or established\, with no age limit. Applicants must be comfortable working
  in French or English. Note: the studio-apartments do not meet current acc
 essibility standards for people with disabilities.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:martin-roth-initiative-relocation-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T205315Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260911
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260912
SUMMARY:Deadline: Martin Roth-Initiative: Temporary Relocation for Artists 
 and Cultural Actors at Risk (Programme Line 1\, 2026 call)
DESCRIPTION:The Martin Roth-Initiative is the German temporary-relocation p
 rogramme for artists and cultural actors at risk\, run jointly by the Goet
 he-Institut and ifa with Federal Foreign Office funding. Programme Line 1 
 relocates an artist to Germany for up to 15 months on a scholarship\, with
  insurance\, language courses\, psychosocial support\, counselling and vis
 a assistance\, plus personnel funding for the hosting organisation. ELIGIB
 ILITY: artists and cultural practitioners anywhere in the world who are de
 monstrably committed through their work to an open society\, freedom\, pea
 ce and democracy\; who face threats\, persecution or unsafe living conditi
 ons\; who have no access to a safe place to continue working\; and who spe
 ak English or German. Applicants must still be active in their home countr
 y or have left it after 20 February 2026. Citizens of EU and EEA countries
 \, Australia\, Canada\, Israel\, New Zealand\, Switzerland\, the UK and th
 e USA are excluded\, as are residents of Gaza and previous MRI recipients.
  HOST REQUIREMENT: applications are submitted jointly with a non-profit ho
 st organisation in Germany (museum\, theatre\, festival\, cultural collect
 ive\, NGO) that is a legal entity able to handle the administrative and di
 gital-security requirements. Note that the scholarship visa does not itsel
 f permit employment or self-employment in Germany. TIMELINE: applications 
 6 July to 11 September 2026\; decisions end of November 2026\; funding sta
 rts no earlier than 15 January 2027. Apply to apply@mri-application.de (en
 crypted email recommended)\; phone +49 30 284491-77.\n\nOrganisation: Mart
 in Roth-Initiative (Goethe-Institut and ifa\, funded by the German Federal
  Foreign Office)\nLocation: Germany (relocation to a German host organisat
 ion). Open to artists and cultural actors worldwide\, with exclusions.\nAw
 ard: Monthly scholarship for the relocated artist\, plus insurance\, langu
 age courses\, psychosocial support\, counselling and training\, visa suppo
 rt\, and personnel funding for the host organisation. No application fee.\
 nDuration: Up to 15 months\, starting no earlier than 15 January 2027\n\nM
 ore: https://www.martin-roth-initiative.de/en/application-programme-line-1
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.martin-roth-initiative.de/en/application-programme-line-1?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Germany (relocation to a German host organisation). Open to artist
 s and cultural actors worldwide\, with exclusions.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:platform-dali-residencies-2027-what-is-real@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T205315Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:Deadline: Platform Dali Open Call for Residencies 2027: What is rea
 l?
DESCRIPTION:Platform Dali launches its first annual Open Call for Residenci
 es as part of its Research and Creation Programme\, with the inaugural 202
 7 edition built around the question 'What is real?'. Artists of any nation
 ality and any discipline are invited to propose a research and creation re
 sidency project developed through close engagement with one of Platform Da
 li's partner scientific institutions: the Barcelona Supercomputing Center 
 (BSC-CNS)\, ICFO (the Institute of Photonic Sciences)\, the Institute of M
 arine Sciences (ICM-CSIC)\, the Institute for High Energy Physics (IFAE)\,
  and the ecosystem of the Barcelona Biomedical Research Park (PRBB)\, incl
 uding the Centre for Genomic Regulation (CRG) and EMBL Barcelona. Five art
 ists are selected\, each hosted by one of the partner institutions. WHAT T
 HE PROGRAMME EXPECTS: research is treated as a creative practice in its ow
 n right\, and residents are explicitly not expected to arrive with a fully
  defined artwork. The residency is designed to support an initial phase of
  open-ended enquiry inside a scientific research environment\, letting que
 stions\, methods and ideas emerge through dialogue and experimentation\; t
 hat research phase then informs the development and production of a new ar
 twork\, so research and creation run as sequential\, interconnected stages
 . TIMELINE: open call launched 2 July 2026\; applications close 7 Septembe
 r 2026 at 23:59 CET\; selected artists notified by November 2026\; residen
 ts publicly announced 2 December 2026. Two residency periods are available
 \, February to April 2027 and September to November 2027\, with final date
 s agreed between Platform Dali\, the host scientific institution and each 
 resident. Full application criteria\, residency structure and terms and co
 nditions are on the open call page.\n\nOrganisation: Platform Dali\nLocati
 on: Barcelona\, Spain\, hosted at one of Platform Dali's partner scientifi
 c institutions. Open to artists of any nationality.\nAward: Artist fee of 
 EUR 7\,500 per selected artist\, plus access to a production budget of up 
 to EUR 25\,000 for the development of a new artwork. Five artists are sele
 cted. For artists based outside Barcelona\, Platform Dali covers travel\, 
 accommodation\, subsistence and travel insurance for both the introductory
  visit and the on-site residency\, within a predefined budget. Also provid
 ed: curatorial support from Platform Dali and the partner institution's te
 am throughout the residency\, and access to the host institution's facilit
 ies\, expertise and research communities\, subject to that institution's r
 egulations and operational requirements. For collectives\, the artist fee\
 , production budget and covered expenses are shared among members\, and a 
 maximum of two members may take part in the introductory visit and on-site
  residency.\nDuration: One of two residency periods: February to April 202
 7\, or September to November 2027. Final dates are agreed between Platform
  Dali\, the host institution and the resident.\n\nMore: https://platformda
 li.org/en/call/open-call-for-residencies-2027-what-is-real/?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://platformdali.org/en/call/open-call-for-residencies-2027-what-is
 -real/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Barcelona\, Spain\, hosted at one of Platform Dali's partner scien
 tific institutions. Open to artists of any nationality.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:archipel-butor-livre-de-dialogue-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T205315Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260830
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260831
SUMMARY:Deadline: Archipel Butor Livre de dialogue Creation Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:Archipel Butor runs its creation residency out of the former ho
 me of the writer Michel Butor in Lucinges\, Haute-Savoie\, and this call i
 s for a livre de dialogue\, a dialogue book made jointly by a writer and a
  visual artist. The residency exists to give a pair concentrated time to d
 evelop a book together and to raise the profile of artist book culture and
  of collaboration at the centre of artistic process. WHO APPLIES: a pair m
 ade up of an author with a project for a dialogue book and a visual artist
  collaborating on it. The two do not need to have worked together before\,
  but both must be present during the shared periods. WHAT IS PROVIDED: EUR
  2\,000 gross per month per artist\, up to two return trips per person wit
 hin France and Europe\, and accommodation in the writer's house. STRUCTURE
 : two months in total\, taken as eight weeks which may be split across the
  year from January 2027\, with 70 percent of the time given to creation an
 d 30 percent to mediation and public engagement activities. A videoconfere
 nce is held with the selected laureates beforehand to arrange on-site sche
 duling and the mediation sessions. HOW TO APPLY: follow the official call 
 document downloadable from the residency page\, submitting a single PDF to
  accueil@archipel-butor.fr containing a joint letter\, biographies of both
  practitioners\, the artistic proposal\, technical specifications and the 
 proposed mediation activities. NOTE: the call and application file are in 
 French. Deadline 30 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Archipel Butor\nLocation
 : Lucinges (74380)\, Haute-Savoie\, France\, in the house of the writer Mi
 chel Butor.\nAward: Creation grant of EUR 2\,000 gross per month per artis
 t\, so roughly EUR 4\,000 each across the two months and EUR 8\,000 for th
 e pair. Up to two return journeys per person are covered within France and
  Europe. Accommodation is provided in Michel Butor's writer's house. No ap
 plication fee.\nDuration: Two months in total\, taken as eight weeks that 
 may be split\, starting from January 2027. Time is split 70 percent creati
 on and 30 percent mediation activities.\n\nMore: https://www.archipel-buto
 r.fr/residence-creation/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
URL:https://www.archipel-butor.fr/residence-creation/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Lucinges (74380)\, Haute-Savoie\, France\, in the house of the wri
 ter Michel Butor.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cultural-horizons-residencies-subgrants-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20260901T205315Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Cultural Horizons Residencies: Subgrants for EU-Ukrainian
  Residency Projects 2027
DESCRIPTION:Cultural Horizons strengthens the cultural sector in Ukraine by
  promoting joint EU-Ukrainian cultural initiatives and expanding access fo
 r Ukrainians affected by the war to cultural and artistic networks in Euro
 pe. Running 2026 to 2027\, it provides subgrants for projects developed th
 rough EU-Ukrainian partnerships and builds a Europe-wide network of cultur
 al expert mentors. THIS CALL\, the Residencies strand\, gives subgrants to
  EU-based institutions to run (a) residency placements and/or (b) educatio
 n projects organised on the basis of residencies\, for and with Ukrainian 
 artistic and cultural professionals during 2027. WHO CAN APPLY: artistic a
 nd cultural organisations and initiatives registered within the EU. Consor
 tium applications are allowed but must designate one lead organisation to 
 submit and manage the funding. This is an organisational call\, so individ
 ual Ukrainian artists cannot apply directly\; they participate as the host
 ed residents. Applicants must show they can host Ukrainian professionals i
 n 2027 and complete the project in the stated window. NGOs and public sect
 or institutions working with displaced and vulnerable groups are prioritis
 ed. CONDITIONS: applicants must confirm the absence of ties with the Russi
 an Federation\, meaning no working partnerships with Russia or Russian org
 anisations and no visits to Russian-occupied territories after 2014\, comm
 it to refrain from the glorification of Russian imperialism\, and comply w
 ith the EU sanctions regime. They must also demonstrate a commitment to di
 versity\, equity and inclusion and provide a working environment based on 
 mutual trust\, awareness and intercultural sensitivity. WHO THE MONEY IS M
 EANT TO REACH: Ukrainian artists and cultural practitioners\, whether inde
 pendent or employed\, including early-career specialists\, debut artists\,
  cultural managers\, researchers\, analysts and conservators\; vulnerable 
 groups from Ukraine including internally displaced persons\, young artists
 \, and communities in frontline and conflict-affected areas\; and cultural
  organisations in Ukraine\, with particular focus on small communities\, l
 ocal initiatives\, independent cultural spaces and NGOs. APPLYING: submiss
 ion is through a JotForm hosted by Cultural Vistas and must be complete\, 
 including uploads\, or it will not be processed. You should receive an ema
 il confirmation\; if it does not arrive\, the submission was not received.
  Enquiries to culturalhorizons@culturalvistas.eu. NOTE ON DATES: the eligi
 bility section says projects must be completed within January to August 20
 27 while the application instructions give the implementation phase as 1 J
 anuary to 30 July 2027\, so plan to the earlier end date. Programme backgr
 ound is at culturalvistas.eu under Our Programs\, Professional Study Tours
 \, Cultural Horizons.\n\nOrganisation: Ukrainian Cultural Foundation and C
 ultural Vistas\, funded by the Creative Europe programme of the European U
 nion\nLocation: Applicant organisations must be registered in the EU. Resi
 dencies are hosted in the EU for Ukrainian artistic and cultural professio
 nals.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 to 20\,000 per subgrant\, with a minimum of 20 su
 bgrants to be awarded. No application fee.\nDuration: Projects run between
  1 January and 30 July 2027\, minimum 3 months and maximum 8 months. Appli
 cations 29 June to 30 September 2026\; evaluation October to November 2026
 . Final reports are due within one month of project completion and no late
 r than 15 August 2027.\n\nMore: https://culturalvistas.jotform.com/2617534
 20662859?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://culturalvistas.jotform.com/261753420662859?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicant organisations must be registered in the EU. Residencies 
 are hosted in the EU for Ukrainian artistic and cultural professionals.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:le-garage-moderne-oasis-residencies-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T205315Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Le Garage Moderne: OASIS International Artist Residencies
  2026 (Bordeaux)
DESCRIPTION:Second year of Le Garage Moderne's residency cycle within the E
 uropean OASIS project\, offering five grants to international artists for 
 two-week stays in Bordeaux. THE SITE IS THE POINT. Le Garage Moderne is a 
 working non-profit car and bicycle workshop with a neighbourhood canteen a
 nd a versatile venue for performing arts\, concerts and community gatherin
 gs\, all at once a productive space\, a public space and a community-drive
 n common. Having just moved back into its 19th-century building after a lo
 ng renovation\, the team describes machines and workbenches back in place 
 and a brand-new playground\, and invites residents to take over the space 
 and explore its physical and social possibilities. They ask for SITE-SPECI
 FIC PROPOSALS that play with the verticality\, the scale of the space\, th
 e community and what they call the hive-like vibe of the venue\, where eve
 ryone runs around\, shouts\, gets their hands dirty and learns in the proc
 ess. DISCIPLINES: any\, explicitly including design\, visual art\, perform
 ing arts\, film\, small-scale architecture\, emergency architecture\, craf
 t-making\, street furniture\, sound\, and interdisciplinary or community-b
 ased practices. Proposals combining artistic creation with the spatial and
  the social are especially encouraged\, and the organisers say plainly tha
 t they want to be surprised. WHAT IS EXPECTED: openness to exchange and co
 llaboration with the 11 permanent residents and with 3 local artists recru
 ited through a separate OASIS call\; participation in 2 days of masterclas
 s open to members and community\, where you describe and share your practi
 ce\, technique and working context with fellow OASIS residents\, local art
 ists\, members and staff\; and a public outcome\, which need not be a larg
 e event but must be something the public can experience. RIGHTS: work prod
 uced during the residency remains the artist's property\, but documentatio
 n of it is made by Le Garage Moderne and will be publicised by them for th
 ree years after the residency. Note this is a different OASIS partner call
  from the OASis In the Park (Naples) and Disappearing Landscape (High Tatr
 as) rounds under the same European project.\n\nOrganisation: Le Garage Mod
 erne (European OASIS project)\nLocation: Bacalan district\, Bordeaux\, Fra
 nce. Le Garage Moderne is a non-profit car garage and bicycle workshop\, a
  canteen serving sponsored meals\, and a cultural venue housing 11 permane
 nt artists\, makers and craftswomen\, recently returned to its 19th-centur
 y building after a two-and-a-half-year renovation.\nAward: Five grants. Ea
 ch artist receives a fee of EUR 1\,300 gross (taxes may apply depending on
  legal status)\, up to EUR 600 for production expenses such as raw materia
 ls\, technical services or special tools\, a lump-sum travel grant scaled 
 to distance with top-ups for green travel options\, a per diem of EUR 45 p
 er day\, and accommodation in a self-catering hotel. Access to the shared 
 tools and spaces of Le Garage Moderne is included\, subject to the associa
 tion's regulations. No application fee.\nDuration: Two weeks on site. Five
  overlapping two-week slots\, and applicants may choose one or more: 9 to 
 22 November\, 16 to 29 November\, 23 November to 6 December\, 30 November 
 to 13 December\, and 7 to 20 December 2026. Deadline 1 September 2026\; pr
 e-selection interviews 15 September\; final selection announced 1 October 
 2026.\n\nMore: https://legaragemoderne.org/oasis2026?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://legaragemoderne.org/oasis2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Bacalan district\, Bordeaux\, France. Le Garage Moderne is a non-p
 rofit car garage and bicycle workshop\, a canteen serving sponsored meals\
 , and a cultural venue housing 11 permanent artists\, makers and craftswom
 en\, recently returned to its 19th-century building after a two-and-a-half
 -year renovation.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kultur-ensemble-palermo-residencies-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T205315Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260906
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260907
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kultur Ensemble Palermo Residencies 2027 (Franco-German D
 uos)
DESCRIPTION:Kultur Ensemble Palermo\, the joint Franco-German cultural inst
 itute uniting the Institut francais Palermo and the Goethe-Institut Palerm
 o since 2021\, offers two three-month residencies promoting research and c
 reation on Franco-German projects with a close link to Palermo and Sicily.
  Residents work from the Bottega\, the 115 sq m artist's studio inaugurate
 d in October 2024 within the Cantieri Culturali alla Zisa. WHO CAN APPLY\,
  and this is the unusual constraint: applications must come from a FRANCO-
 GERMAN DUO\, meaning French or German nationality or working in France or 
 Germany\, and all applicants must be UNDER 36 at the time of the residency
 \, a requirement of the Franco-German Youth Office which funds the scheme.
  Beyond that\, applicants need a practice or project that genuinely justif
 ies the need for a studio\, and a project related to Palermo\, Sicily or t
 he Mediterranean region. COMMITMENTS: participate in at least two educatio
 nal activities such as a presentation of work or a workshop with Palermo s
 chools\; provide communication material for the institutes' social media a
 nd take part in a short video interview\; be free from other professional 
 commitments during the residency\; and hold civil liability insurance and 
 health insurance valid abroad for the full period. A public presentation e
 vent is NOT mandatory and can be discussed with the institutes during the 
 stay. The institutes also help establish contacts with the local cultural 
 network and institutions. APPLYING: all documents in a single PDF\, submit
 ted in duplicate\, one version in French or German and one in English\, to
  kulturensemblepalermo@gmail.com. Required: CV of maximum 2 pages per pers
 on for everyone involved including contact details and date of birth\; a p
 roject description with justification for the studio\, maximum 1 page\; an
 d a portfolio of maximum 10 pages total. An Italian-French-German jury of 
 experts decides at the end of September 2026\, with results announced by e
 mail and published on Kultur Ensemble Palermo's Instagram and the social c
 hannels of both institutes. NOTE ON DATES: the official English call PDF s
 ays 'two three-month residencies in 2026'\, which is an error carried into
  several republished versions. The residency periods listed in the same do
 cument\, and the French institute's own page\, both give 2027. Enquiries: 
 bianca.bozzeda@goethe.de (Goethe-Institut) or judith.testault@institutfran
 cais.it (Institut francais).\n\nOrganisation: Kultur Ensemble Palermo (Ins
 titut francais Palermo and Goethe-Institut Palermo)\, with the Franco-Germ
 an Youth Office (OFAJ/DFJW)\nLocation: Palermo\, Sicily. Studio at the Bot
 tega\, a 115 sq m space within the Cantieri Culturali alla Zisa\, shared w
 ith other residents.\nAward: Two residencies. Each provides a residency gr
 ant of EUR 1\,500 per person per month\, one return journey between home a
 nd Palermo capped at EUR 500 per person\, a budget of up to EUR 500 for re
 search\, creation and production costs (agreed in advance with the institu
 tes)\, and accommodation in the city with private rooms and shared common 
 spaces. Over three months that is EUR 4\,500 per person in grant alone\, a
 nd duos are funded per person. No application fee.\nDuration: Three months
 . Two slots in 2027: 11 January to 4 April\, and 20 September to 12 Decemb
 er. Deadline 6 September 2026 at midnight\; jury decision end of September
  2026.\n\nMore: https://www.institutfrancais.it/fr/palerme/bando-residenze
 -il-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.institutfrancais.it/fr/palerme/bando-residenze-il-2027?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Palermo\, Sicily. Studio at the Bottega\, a 115 sq m space within 
 the Cantieri Culturali alla Zisa\, shared with other residents.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:unidee-cittadellarte-ecosystems-living-communities-vol3@artificialnouve
 au.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T205315Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260906
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260907
SUMMARY:Deadline: Ecosystems as Living Communities vol. III: UniCredit Grou
 p UNIDEE Connective Residencies 2026-27
DESCRIPTION:Third edition of Ecosystems as Living Communities\, supporting 
 two production residencies for emerging international artists working with
  socially engaged practices that address contemporary ecological issues. T
 WO PLACES\, and the split matters: one Italian artist and one internationa
 l artist residing in Europe. The framing follows the mission of Fondazione
  Pistoletto Cittadellarte\, the vision and work of Michelangelo Pistoletto
 \, and the UN Sustainable Development Goals\, and promotes interdisciplina
 ry collaboration across scientific\, technological and humanistic fields. 
 WHAT THEY WANT: projects that investigate ecosystems as interconnected com
 munities of humans and non-humans\, challenging anthropocentric perspectiv
 es and promoting an ecocentric mindset\, and that foster positive and rege
 nerative visions of desirable futures rather than only diagnosing crisis. 
 HOW IT RUNS: the two artists share a research phase including meetings wit
 h tutors\, researchers and experts as well as field visits\, so a collabor
 ative attitude and flexibility as the research evolves are described as es
 sential. Resulting works are publicly presented at Cittadellarte in Biella
  and disseminated online. IMPORTANT ON RIGHTS: the final artwork produced 
 during the residency BECOMES PART OF THE UNICREDIT ART COLLECTION\, so thi
 s is a production residency that ends in acquisition by a corporate collec
 tion\, not a no-strings creation grant. Weigh that against the fee before 
 applying. For large installations\, artists are also required to develop a
  simplified version of the work that can be installed in smaller exhibitio
 n spaces while preserving its conceptual integrity. APPLYING: complete the
  online form and submit the required documents\, all in English\, includin
 g a portfolio and CV as one PDF up to 5 MB containing a selected portfolio
  of maximum 5 projects or artworks most fitting to the call topic\, plus a
  brief biography and CV.\n\nOrganisation: Fondazione Pistoletto Cittadella
 rte and UNIDEE Residency Programs\, in collaboration with UniCredit Group\
 nLocation: Cittadellarte\, Biella\, Italy.\nAward: Two residencies. Each p
 rovides a gross artist fee of EUR 6\,500\, a production budget of up to EU
 R 2\,500 for costs directly related to producing the final artwork (instal
 lation supports\, equipment rental\, materials)\, round-trip travel and re
 search trips with a combined budget of EUR 1\,000 to 1\,500 per artist dep
 ending on distance\, accommodation in a single room with shared facilities
  at Cittadellarte plus a per diem of EUR 25 per day for up to 60 days\, an
 d a research budget of up to EUR 500 for fees to experts contributing to t
 he research. Cittadellarte separately covers technical support for the exh
 ibition installation\, project communication\, and a publication accompany
 ing the residency and final exhibition. No application fee.\nDuration: Res
 idencies take place between December 2026 and April 2027. The structure an
 d schedule are tailored to each project and defined collaboratively with t
 he artists. Deadline 6 September 2026 at 23:59\; shortlisted candidates ma
 y be interviewed online between late September and mid-October\; selection
  by mid-October 2026.\n\nMore: https://unidee.cittadellarte.it/activity.ht
 ml?id=263&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://unidee.cittadellarte.it/activity.html?id=263&utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Cittadellarte\, Biella\, Italy.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
